| `agents.max_session_model_calls` | integer | `0` | a whole number, 0 or more | `models/budget.py` (`approved_session_cap`, `SessionBudget`, `check_session_total`); `mcp/qa_server.py` (`configured_session_cap`) | The approved cap on the model calls one `mcp/qa_server.py` process makes across all its questions, from start to exit, read once at start. A question is admitted only when its `agents.max_model_calls`, added to the calls the process has already made, stays within this total; otherwise `wiki_answer` returns a tool error naming this key, the total and the calls made, and makes no model call. Every call a question makes is counted, one that fails included, so the count is the calls made, not the bounds admitted. Restarting the server starts the count at 0. `0` admits no question that may make a call: a long-lived server is the spend risk, a per-question cap alone never bounds it, and a total keel picked would be a spend no owner approved, so the owner sets both. Absent, the reader writes `[using default] agents.max_session_model_calls = 0` to stderr; a value that is not a whole number of 0 or more stops the server with exit 14 before it serves, and so does a nonzero total below `agents.max_model_calls`, the line naming both keys and their values, since no question could fit it (`models.check_session_total`). | each question's own bound: `agents.max_model_calls`; an agent CLI's run, which ends with its process and so has no session | always |
